    "frames": [
      {
        "slide": 1,
        "role": "cover",
        "subject": "An evening aerial over a Gulf Coast subdivision. Three big near roofs are cut by the bottom edge, the centre one stripped to tan decking with a blue sandbagged tarp. Every roof carries a hollow cool rim. A live oak lies uprooted across the street, root plate showing, and one gold tube route bends around its crown and leaves the right edge.",
        "visual_consequence": "A storm-hit street where every roof has been outlined, and one gold line that swerves around the fallen tree and carries on out of frame. With the glow lowered the tube renders as saturated gold rather than pale lemon and stays the brightest, warmest thing in the frame, one continuous way through at 432 px.",
        "weakness": "A thin lime-white seam along the tube's underside where it crosses the curb, and a few debris planks pass through the tube. Both about 2 px at feed size.",
